*Notes:* This table reports the owner–employee gap for large employers (owners with employees and 20 or more people at their workplace), relative to employees of large workplaces of the same origin, from the regressions of @eq-owner-inc in @tbl-b2-main. Panel A reports the gap, $\theta_L$ for the native-born and $\theta_L + \theta_{Lg}$ for migrant group $g$. Panel B reports the difference from the native-born gap, $\theta_{Lg}$, and Panel C its minimum detectable difference, $2.8 \times \text{SE}(\theta_{Lg})$. The dependent variables are income in dollars, and volatility and large falls in percentage points. Each column represents a separate regression on the unrestricted or restricted sample, with the covariates and fixed effects of @tbl-b2-main. The last column is the number of distinct large employers in the restricted income regression. A dash marks the single low-English large employer, who is excluded from estimation. All standard errors reported in parentheses are clustered at the individual and industry-year levels. ∗ p < 0.10, ∗∗ p < 0.05, ∗∗∗ p < 0.01.
:::


