*Notes:* This table reports the owner–employee gap for own-account workers (self-employed, or owners without employees, in small workplaces), relative to employees of small workplaces of the same origin, from the regressions of @eq-owner-inc in @tbl-b2-main. Panel A reports the gap, $\theta_O$ for the native-born and $\theta_O + \theta_{Og}$ for migrant group $g$. Panel B reports the difference from the native-born gap, $\theta_{Og}$, and Panel C its minimum detectable difference, $2.8 \times \text{SE}(\theta_{Og})$. The dependent variables are income in dollars, and volatility and large falls in percentage points. Each column represents a separate regression on the unrestricted or restricted sample, with the covariates and fixed effects of @tbl-b2-main. The last column is the number of distinct own-account workers in the restricted income regression. All standard errors reported in parentheses are clustered at the individual and industry-year levels. ∗ p < 0.10, ∗∗ p < 0.05, ∗∗∗ p < 0.01.
