*Notes:* This table reports unconditional entry into business ownership in the transition sample, by origin group. The entry rate is the percentage of at-risk person-pairs (not a business owner at $t-1$) in which the individual owns a business at $t$. The 95% confidence interval is from a bootstrap that resamples individuals (2,000 replications). *p vs Australian-born* is from a Fisher exact test; a chi-square test of equal rates across all groups gives p < 0.001. *Standardised rate* is the entry rate each group would have with the Australian-born mix of age band and industry of most recent job at $t-1$, computed as each group's average predicted entry rate over the Australian-born person-pairs from a logit of entry on origin group, age band and industry.
